Push auth was already done; what is open is the spoke's own read identity
==========================================================================
Date : 2026-08-02
Mode : LIVE against the real hub route (`local_deploy_api:/api/platform/status`)
Gate : make check 1614 -> 1617 (+3)

Plan item : NEXT_PLAN 2차 잔여 "agent→hub push 인증"
Outcome   : that item is STALE — done 2026-07-26, re-measured here. The real
            remaining piece is a different one and now says so.


1. The write side is enforced, and was already enforced
---------------------------------------------------------
Hub started with two per-identity keys, then five attempts against the real route:

    ① acme key, own rows only          : 200 ACCEPTED
    ② no signature header              : 401 {"detail":"report rejected"}
    ③ signed with the wrong key        : 401 {"detail":"report rejected"}
    ④ globex's key claiming acme/dev   : 401 {"detail":"report rejected"}
    ⑤ acme's key carrying a globex row : 401 {"detail":"report signed by acme/dev
                                              carries rows for ['globex/dev']"}

②③④ share one message on purpose — distinguishing "no such tenant" from "wrong
key" would leak the tenant list. All of this landed 2026-07-26 (gate 1219→1251,
`phase2-push-collector-and-switcher.log` §4). NEXT_PLAN has listed it as remaining
work for a week.

A NOTE ON MEASURING: the first run of ⑤ returned 200 and looked like a real hole.
It was not — the probe sent its rows under an `addons` key while `StatusReport`
reads `statuses`, so the rows never parsed and an empty report was legitimately
accepted. Recorded rather than tidied away, because a false finding from a
malformed fixture is the mirror image of the defect this repo keeps hunting: the
fixture has to be the shape the real producer sends (`to_dict()`), or the
experiment measures nothing.


2. The read side is not bounded by a credential
--------------------------------------------------
    src/agents/platform/collector.py
      def _kubectl(*args): subprocess.run(["kubectl", *args], ...)

No `--kubeconfig`, no `--context` — the same shape D38 found on the deploy path
and closed there. Three consequences, none of them previously written down:

  * `read_applications` reads `applications.argoproj.io -n argocd`. That namespace
    is SHARED: it holds every tenant's Applications. Confinement to one tenant
    happens afterwards, in Python, by label — so on the read path the boundary is
    code, not the credential.
  * there is no in-cluster manifest for the spoke. `infra/helm/platform-agent/
    templates/` ships router, webhook, orphan-sweeper, rbac, pvc — no status
    pusher. The agent runs from the Makefile (`make dev-up`, `--interval 60`)
    against the operator's ambient context, which on kind is cluster-admin.
  * so the module's opening claim — "each cluster runs an agent that reads only
    itself" — describes an intended deployment, not the one that exists.

The docstring also said "a spoke agent's blast radius is one tenant/env on the read
path too". That sentence has been replaced with what is actually true: the hub
bounds what a spoke can WRITE; nothing bounds what it can READ.


3. What shipped
-----------------
`warn_if_ambient_read()` — the process says once, not once a minute, that its
cluster read is ambient and that the boundary is not the credential. `_kubectl`
calls it, so the statement cannot drift away from the behaviour.

Warning, not refusal, for the reason D38 already settled: fail-closed here breaks
`make dev-up` and the two-line demo, and a boundary nobody can run is the failure
mode this repo documented once already. No credential seam was added either — D38
shipped its seam together with `make deploy-identity` to mint against, and adding
an env var nobody can populate would be that same defect with a new name.

Guards (`tests/test_push_read_identity.py`), each falsified individually:
    let `_kubectl` bypass the warning        -> "the cluster read did not announce
                                                its identity"
    soften the wording to "default kubeconfig" -> "the warning must name what is
                                                NOT enforced"
    remove the once-per-process latch          -> "says it once, not once a minute"


4. Still open (recorded in NEXT_PLAN, not invented here)
----------------------------------------------------------
A scoped read identity for the spoke needs two things this repo does not have yet:
an in-cluster deployment for the pusher, and a ServiceAccount whose RBAC is narrow
enough to be worth the claim. Both are infrastructure decisions, and the second
only means something once the first exists.


Reproduce
-----------
  PLATFORM_PUSH_KEYS='{"acme/dev":"k1","globex/dev":"k2"}' \
    uvicorn src.agents.ai.local_deploy_api:app --port 8137
  # sign with collector.sign(report.to_dict(), key) and POST to /api/platform/status
  python -m pytest tests/test_push_read_identity.py -v
